    {
      "id": "claim_2ce38c486f6c45f6ac4280c4206faf63",
      "statement": "scripts/__tests__/wiki-maintain.guard.test.mjs asserts three things together for the pinned generation model: the explicit OPENWIKI_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS cap is set and at or above the 16384-token minimum a page-writing turn needs, OpenWiki's own resolveAnthropicMaxOutputTokens regex still matches OPENWIKI_MODEL_ID, and that id would not resolve to @langchain/anthropic's 4096-token fallback if the explicit cap were removed. Two of its four cap-related tests skip (rather than fail) when OpenWiki is not installed under the global node_modules path, so a skip can misleadingly read as a pass; the claude-sonnet-5 bump was verified at 20 passed / 0 failed / 0 skipped.",
